  "result": {
    "summary": "Synchronized collection improved all three terminal generic-anchor cells and the mean by +266.58 bb/100 versus matched sequential, but increased seat-node log imbalance from 3.236 to 3.960 because sampled preflop folds yielded zero P0 traverser nodes in later iterations.",
    "conclusion": "Iteration synchronization removes a real ordering confound but is not sufficient at tiny budgets without exploration support. Terminal-current evaluation is also not the SD-CFR average-strategy contract.",
    "decision": "REJECT_SYNCHRONIZATION_AS_SUFFICIENT_FIX",
    "next_step": "Add explicit recorded epsilon opponent exploration and iteration-weighted per-hand strategy-snapshot evaluation; compare epsilon0 versus0.1 under synchronized common-deck collection and require nonzero coverage plus improved balance."
